const template = generateEmailTemplate('welcome', {
  firstName: 'John',
  lastName: 'Doe',
  email: 'john@example.com',
  // ... other attributes
});

// Send email using your email service
await emailService.send({
  to: user.email,
  subject: template.subject,
  html: template.html,
  text: template.text
});
```

## Security Notes

- All user attributes are treated as untrusted input
- HTML escaping prevents XSS attacks through user names, companies, etc.
- Rich text is sanitized server-side before being included in emails
- URL protocols are validated to prevent javascript: and data: URI attacks
- No user input is ever concatenated into executable code
